    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1176">

                <pb facs="0959" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg843"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/6951.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Secretary of the Navy</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 20, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to recent telegrams from Admiral
                    Winslow, copies of which have been sent to this Department, in regard to the
                    situation at Los Mochis, Mexico, I have the honor to inform you that Mr. John R.
                    Silliman was given telegraphic instructions last night to urge upon General
                    Venustiano Carranza the importance of furnishing adequate protection for
                    American life and property at Los Mochis.</p>
                <pb facs="0960" n="844" xml:id="pg844"/>
                <p>In this connection, I have the honor to request that Admiral Winslow be
                    instructed by telegraph to keep the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Annapolis</hi> at Topolobampo until order has been restored at Los
                    Mochis.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
